>[In particular, sendmail is logging to & from addresses in
>/var/adm/syslog, which is publicly-readable.

This is pretty standard practice on Unix machines running sendmail.
Often the log is kept in /usr/spool/mqueue/syslog (and syslog.0,
syslog.1, etc.).  The file will be world-readable by default unless the
system adminstrator makes it otherwise, I believe.

Just because it's standard practice doesn't mean it's a good idea,
of course.

On some systems I've used, the outgoing mail queue (/usr/spool/mqueue/*)
is also publicly readable!  That's a serious breach of privacy.
